  "question": {
    "text": "A block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is in equilibrium after being suspended from the ceiling with the help of a spring of force constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>. The block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>,&nbsp;strikes the block&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;and sticks to it. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the spring&nbsp;just attains its natural length is<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0026_21b9c5b278e6.jpg\" style=\"width: 100px; height: 195px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
